    "done_when": "Write the tangent of every polygonanalytic vertex term the Biot point jet differentiates, under the locked decisions kernel-loop-representation = custom-derivative-rules and tangent-identity-tolerance = scan-tangents-1e-9 on converged-forward-solve. The elliptic, range-function, moment-channel and graded-residual tangents have landed (nova/biot/elliptic.py, completeelliptic.py, rangefunction.py, momentchannel.py, gradedresidual.py, with tests/biot/test_elliptic_tangent_recurrences.py, test_range_tangent_recurrences.py and test_vertex_edge_tangent_recurrences.py as the pattern); reuse them, never re-derive them. Done when: (0) the jaxpr of packed_analytic_moments (nova/biot/polygonanalytic.py) is enumerated for every source kind the point jet takes, listing each nova/biot function reached with its staged call count and whether a private tangent already exists, written to a log in the run directory and tabulated in the fragment; (1) private tangents for the vertex quantities: the _Vertex construction, _first_residual, arsinh_terms, flux_moment_residuals, horizontal_flux_line_moments, and the corner_part constructions that build a _Vertex, each returning the same structure jax.jvp returns with respect to all floating inputs without calling jax.jvp, jax.grad or jax.jacfwd on the base; (2) identity on 10,000 random vertex geometries and targets spanning the domain the jet forms, targets beside a vertex and beside an edge included, no masking, each tangent within relative 1e-13 of jax.jvp of the base for exact forms and 1e-9 for scan forms, maxima and covered fraction printed, covered fraction 100 percent; where the base jax.jvp is not finite, compare against an mpmath reference at 50 digits and say so, or cite the guard in nova/biot that keeps the jet from forming that input and narrow the sampled domain to it; (3) negative control: each tangent with one recurrence or product-rule term dropped under NOVA_TANGENT_TRUNCATION=1 fails that identity, maximum